dle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">S100A9</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">16.1 &#x000b1; 4.4</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">17.1 &#x000b1; 3.1</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">9.8 &#x000b1; 2.0</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">23.6 &#x000b1; 5.6<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="TFN3">*</xref></td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">12.7 &#x000b1; 2.7</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">28.8 &#x000b1; 6.9<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="TFN3">*</xref></td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="TFN1"><label>a</label><p id="P29">Final transcript data were normalized to 18S rRNA and presented as [(molecules of transcript/molecules of 18S rRNA) &#x000d7; 10<sup>-5</sup>]. Values shown are mean &#x000b1; SE.</p></fn><fn id="TFN2"><label>b</label><p id="P30">Deep myometrial invasion is defined as invasion greater than or equal to 50% myometrial wall thickness.</p></fn><fn id="TFN3"><label>*</label><p id="P31">p&#x0003c;0.05</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></sec></back></article>